# Wrap prior art

When a named upstream tool already implements the mechanism (CLI, protocol,
store format), **pin an unmodified copy** and put org/repo/git/CI behavior in a
**wrapper**. Do not rewrite the upstream in-tree to “make it ours.”

## Do

- Record the pin (git SHA and content hash) next to the vendored file.
- Extend through the hook the tool already ships (`MEMORY_DIR`, flags, env,
  subprocess). If it has no hook, wrap it; do not patch its source.
- Teach agents the **wrapper** path in `AGENTS.md`, not a rewritten clone.

## Do not

- Copy an unlicensed or third-party program and then edit it as if it were ours.
- Reimplement a cover/log/tree/engine “inspired by” an upstream that we already
  vendor.
- Relicense third-party files. Note rights in `THIRD_PARTY.md` when there is no
  license.

This repository’s OptMem integration is the instance: `optmem/upstream/memo` is
immutable; `optmem/repo-memo` is the layer.
